+ * and {@code HASH8} is the first 8 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over
+ * {@code normalizedTelephone + lastName} (e.g. {@code NSW-1A2B3C4D}).
+ *
+ * <p>The identity is deterministic from the owner's own fields alone — there is no per-city
+ * sequence number any more, so it no longer depends on how many owners already exist. The
+ * telephone is taken in its canonical E.164 form ({@link OwnerTelephone#toE164(String)}, the same
+ * normalisation {@link NormalizeOwnerTelephone} already applied upstream) so the hash is stable
+ * regardless of how the number was originally formatted.
+ *
+ * <p>This {@code customerCode} is the single region-and-hash identity every derived owner value
